{"test":"text:nat_en.txt","n_prompt":113,"pp_s":6.572,"pp_ts":17.1934,"n_gen":128,"tg_ts":6.1289,"tg_total_ts":6.1117,"gen":"The storm came in three waves. The first was a wall of water that lifted the boat from its moorings and hurled it against the rocks. The second wave was the wind, which howled through the lighthouse and sent the door slamming open and shut. The third wave was the sea itself, which rose up and took the lighthouse, and the man, and the lamp, and the logbook, and the gulls, and the rocks, and the sky, and the sea, and the night, and the wind, and the dark, and the silence, and the sound, and the time, and the place"}
